1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
MutantReview mutation-tests code changed in a merge request.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,600
Here, I run its real engine on the checkout demo.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:14,060
Vitest and Stryker are running. This wait is sped up 5×.

4
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:19,230
The baseline tests pass with 100% branch coverage.

5
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:24,230
But one mutation survives: changing >= to > goes undetected.

6
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:28,060
The 80% score is below the 90% policy, so the gate fails.

7
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:33,230
The finding identifies the exact $100 free-shipping boundary.

8
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:39,160
The contract says orders of at least $100 ship free.

9
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:44,230
First, I propose a test for an order of $100.01.

10
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:49,230
MutantReview executes it on the original code and the mutant.

11
00:00:49,230 --> 00:00:54,110
It passes on both, so the repair is rejected.

12
00:00:54,110 --> 00:00:59,230
Now I propose a test at exactly $100, or 10,000 cents.

13
00:00:59,230 --> 00:01:04,230
Zero shipping comes from the written requirement, not the implementation.

14
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:09,860
This test passes on the original and kills the exact mutation.

15
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:15,230
I inspect the verified proposal before changing the test file.

16
00:01:15,230 --> 00:01:20,560
These are the actual finding, contract, and proposed assertion.

17
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:25,030
I apply that verified test to the local checkout.

18
00:01:25,030 --> 00:01:28,760
The updated test file is printed, and a fresh review starts.

19
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:32,620
Stryker reruns the mutations. Execution is sped up 3.5×.

20
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:37,230
Now all five tests pass, and every mutation is caught.

21
00:01:37,230 --> 00:01:41,320
The real gate command returns passed with exit code zero.

22
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:46,730
The dashboard shows 100% mutation score and zero surviving mutants.

23
00:01:46,730 --> 00:01:52,230
Here is the added boundary test in the actual test file.

24
00:01:52,230 --> 00:01:58,817
MutantReview found the gap, rejected a weak fix, and proved the repair.
